    "summary": "Single-span simply supported precast prestressed small-box girder bridge (30 m bearing-to-bearing, 10 m deck, 9 m carriageway, two-way, 2 lanes, Highway Class II, JTG D60-2015).\n\nModel: 2D spine beam (structure.idealization = spine_beam_2d, system = simply_supported). Girder: 3 small-box girders merged into one beam — single midspan section A = 1.1389 m², I = 0.35492 m⁴ (integrated from the given geometry, void deducted), combined A = 3.4168 m², I = 1.06475 m⁴; C40 → Ec = 32500 MPa; γ = 26.0 kN/m³ (JTGD60-4.2.1), w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.0557 kN·s²/m². Supports: two abutments on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end → 6 per line; 300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers): S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, vertical spring / longitudinal spring / rotation free. Loads: qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk(span 1) = 240 kN, ξ = 1.0 (2 lanes), μ = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.40 Hz (JTGD60-4.3.2).\n\nRoot cause of the initial model_checks failure: the instance bearing records for both abutments carried \"fixed\": true, contradicting the description (plain laminated elastomeric bearings are not longitudinally fixed). This made the assembled model over-constrained/inconsistent, and generate_model failed with no traceable suspect. Correcting the instance to \"fixed\": false (keeping family laminated_elastomeric, sliding false) resolved it.\n\nVerified results after repair: self-weight support reactions 1332.55 + 1332.55 = 2665.09 kN = γ·A·L; first three vertical frequencies 3.40, 13.49, 29.88 Hz; self-weight midspan moment 9994 kN·m; governing lane-load span moment +6449.6 kN·m. Model passes its L1/L2/L3 checks."
